A/B: env-backed u-boot bootcount on R3 (mt7986), foundation for A/B rollback.

Mirror of bpi-r4 z02. Adds BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT/ENV/ALTBOOTCMD to R3's three media
defconfigs, after the AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR line z01 adds. The counter is gated by
the `upgrade_available` env var, so steady-state boots neither count nor write
flash; once it exceeds `bootlimit`, autoboot runs altbootcmd (slot switch).

--- a/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-emmc_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-emmc_defconfig
@@ -23,3 +23,6 @@
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR=" "
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD=y
 CONFIG_OF_SYSTEM_SETUP=y
--- a/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-sd_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-sd_defconfig
@@ -23,3 +23,6 @@
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR=" "
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD=y
 CONFIG_OF_SYSTEM_SETUP=y
--- a/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-snand_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-snand_defconfig
@@ -20,3 +20,6 @@
